    "body": "Let $S$ be the part of the circular paraboloid $z=x^{2}+y^{2}$ below the plane $z=4$ with upward orientation. Let $\\overrightarrow{\\mathbf{F}}(x, y, z)=x z \\overrightarrow{\\mathbf{j}}+y z \\overrightarrow{\\mathbf{k}}$. Compute $\\iint_{S} \\operatorname{curl} \\overrightarrow{\\mathbf{F}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathbf{n}} d S$. Hint: You may need to use one or both of these integrals: $\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}(\\cos t)^{2} d t=\\pi$ and $\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}(\\sin t)^{2} d t=\\pi$.",
